DECISIONS 362, CODEGEN.md §3.5, §5.2: a C++ opened enum is a class holding its wire in `wire_`, its members static members of it: an enumerator named like the enum meets the class's constructor, one named wire_ meets its storage, each E8005 at the member. Closed, neither collides.
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// A destination.
enum Dst { Dst, sta }

/// A mode.
enum Mode { wire_, off }

emit cpp { out: "@features/a/cpp", namespace: "a", mode: types, open: [Dst, Mode] }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8005]  a/a.canon:5:12
  cpp: Dst is generated for both a.Dst and a.Dst.Dst; rename one of them with @cpp(name:)

error[E8005]  a/a.canon:8:13
  cpp: wire_ is generated for both a.Mode and a.Mode.wire_; rename one of them with @cpp(name:)

2 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
